{
  "_doc": [
    "Profiles for scripts/havok/gr2_lint.py. 'references' = numbers MEASURED on vanilla models (python scripts/havok/gr2_lint.py --measure-reference <vanilla.gr2>, files extracted to a scratchpad, never into the repo); never on a pilot or on the model under test.",
    "'profiles' = one building each: its files, the reference it must match, and its own design facts (platform height, props on the fixed base bone) with the reason for each tolerance.",
    "Frames: 'raw' = the gr2 file's own coordinates (y up). 'display' = (-x_raw, -z_raw, y_raw): +X right, +Y back, +Z up, as rotate_gr2.py documents. Quadrants are display-frame, relative to the footprint (bbox) centre."
  ],
  "tools": {
    "gr2_to_raw_dir": "$AOP_KOREAN_REPO/research/Texturing_11/Export_CP1/tools",
    "_doc": "gr2_to_raw.py (headless Granny DLL read under Wine/WSL). Override: env GR2_LINT_TOOLS or config/tool-paths.local.json tools.gr2_to_raw_dir. Missing -> the dll_read check is SKIP, never PASS.",
    "owner_messages": "config/gr2_uv_contracts/owner_authorization.json",
    "_owner_messages_doc": "the owner's message store: a waiver in a profile's \"waivers\" counts only when its owner_quote is one of his WHOLE messages there (as the UV lineage gate). Override: config/tool-paths.local.json tools.owner_messages. Missing -> no waiver counts."
  },
  "texture_budget": {
    "_doc": "AoP texture CEILINGS (this project only; owner 2026-09-30 m334, classes m335/m336; KTC-165). gr2_lint check texture_budget counts a model's own texture SETS (one per BaseColor; the sizes from the DDT headers) against its class. The class is set PER MODEL with the owner: a profile's texture_budget {class, confirmed_by: owner message id, models: [the model stems it covers]}; per_model entries (keyed by the model stem) override it. A class without confirmed_by is PROPOSED and FAILS the export: 'class not confirmed by the owner'. INC-033: confirmed_by must resolve to his message in the store (tools.owner_messages) that names the class and the model (the entry's or profile's \"names\"); a confirmed folder class covers only its \"models\" (the market folder also holds a house and a port); every own texture file of every stage and variant counts, and the animfile's replacetexture targets. The universal UV density floor is not here: .claude/skills/blender-architecture-texturing/references/uv-density-floor.md.",
    "owner_quote": "Model like Town center: 1x2048 + 1x1024 as complementary with transparent objects MAX! Smaller buildings like Barracks: 1x2048 Large buildings (cathedral, Basilica, some bigger woonder): 2x2048 These are ceilings for this project!!!!!!!!!!!!!! (m334)",
    "classes": {
      "small": {
        "ceiling": [
          2048
        ],
        "_doc": "1x2048: barracks-size and smaller (the house is small, m336)"
      },
      "medium": {
        "ceiling": [
          2048,
          1024
        ],
        "_doc": "1x2048 + one 1024 complement for the transparent / cutout objects: Town Center, Market, possibly others per model (m335). Only medium has the complement"
      },
      "large": {
        "ceiling": [
          2048,
          2048
        ],
        "_doc": "2x2048: cathedral, basilica, the bigger wonders"
      }
    },
    "count_shared_vanilla": false,
    "_count_doc": "PROPOSED (gates/BUDGET_INVENTORY.md, 2026-09-30), owner to confirm: shared vanilla atlases a model borrows (generic props, the destruction sheet) are listed by the check but not counted - vanilla's own West TC age 3 loads three sets that way. Also to confirm: '1x2048' is counted as sets with a size cap (implemented), not as a pixel sum."
  },
